# Command palette open-lag receipt, condition 2 of 4: PALETTE OPEN, idle.
#
# The reported symptom: cost tied to the OPEN STATE, not to opening and not to
# typing. Nothing is edited and nothing is selected after the palette opens —
# every measured frame here is the palette merely sitting there. The done
# condition says this block should provoke no repeated state, layout, or raster
# work, so `suggestion_runs`, `chrome_syncs`, and `dirty_tiles` across it are as
# much the receipt as the milliseconds are.
#
# MEASURED BLOCK: the trailing `settle 140`, which is 141 frames. The harness
# skips the one frame `log` costs and reads the 120 before it.
settle 30
key escape
open mere://alpha
open mere://beta
settle 20
assert visible
omnibar actions
assert omnibar open
settle 140
log palette lag: open idle sample complete
